From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tseng <tseng.jayj@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wallet: remove the remaining automatic sensitive log payloads

Patch 0005 removed the routine tools::detail::print_source_entry helper. A
full-tree audit found equivalent INHERITED disclosures still linked into
meepcoin-wallet-cli and meepcoin-wallet-rpc, on exceptional and legacy paths
rather than the routine one. They are removed here.

src/cryptonote_core/cryptonote_tx_utils.cpp
  - miner coinbase construction logged the transaction SECRET key on a
    key-derivation failure;
  - the input bounds failure logged src_entr.real_output, the true ring
    position;
  - the derived-key mismatch failure logged the ring index, the true ring
    position, the derived key, the real output public key, the amount, the
    RCT status, the real out tx key and real_output_in_tx_index -- a
    complete deanonymisation of that input in one error path;
  - the tx.version == 1 path accumulated every ring public key, every ring
    signature, the input EPHEMERAL SECRET KEY and the true ring position
    into a stringstream and emitted it with MCINFO("construct_tx", ...);
  - both construct_tx paths dumped the whole constructed transaction as
    JSON under "transaction_created:" automatically.

src/wallet/wallet2.cpp
  - light_wallet_key_image_is_ours logged the account VIEW SECRET KEY and,
    a few lines later, the derived EPHEMERAL SECRET KEY on failure.

src/device/device_default.cpp
  - output construction logged the TRANSACTION PRIVATE KEY on failure.

Only the payloads are removed. Each site keeps generic failure text that
still says which check failed, so a failure is still diagnosable, and no
site is merely demoted to a lower log level. The dead idx counter that
only the deleted mismatch log used is removed with it.

NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: simplewallet's rpc_payment_info prints the RPC
client secret key because the operator explicitly asked for it. That is a
requested display, not automatic logging, and it is out of scope here.

Control flow, validation, transaction construction, output selection,
consensus, MeepHash, rewards, difficulty, the browser and the native helper
are unchanged. No consensus value moves; construct_tx still builds the same
transaction and still refuses the same inputs.
---
 src/cryptonote_core/cryptonote_tx_utils.cpp | 22 +++------------------
 src/device/device_default.cpp               |  3 +--
 src/wallet/wallet2.cpp                      |  4 ++--
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

